description:
Design a robotic arm controller that utilizes a clock and a button input to manage the arm's position. The controller has a 2-bit wide register representing the current position of the arm, which cycles through positions 0 to 3 (00 to 11 in binary). Upon pressing the button, the arm moves to the next position in the sequence; when it reaches position 4 (100), it resets back to position 0. The position information is then used to drive an output through a specific logic gate (O21BA), which produces the final output signal based on the current position and button state.
